-- title:
--   Configured representative of a finite p-torsion class at p
-- statement:
--   Setting and data. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. The hypothesis `hHp` requires that every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ with $\mathrm{unitsMap}(u) = 1$ for the divisibility $(M/p) \mid M$ lies in $H$, i.e. $H$ contains the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. A set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ is taken as a parameter; it occurs in no other hypothesis and not in the conclusion. The hypothesis `hin : HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H` is the conjunction of the predicate `HeckeInputsHAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for level $(M,H)$ and every prime $\ell$, together with the existence, for each $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{F}_H :=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d`. Further, $\mathrm{Pl}$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hPl : Pl.LiesOverPrime p`, that is $p$ lies in the non-units of $\mathrm{Pl}$, and its residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField ↥Pl` is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$; `hj` says that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of level $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   The remaining data are: an integral model datum $\mathfrak{X} :$ `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` over $R_p =$ `ratLocalizedAt p` (properness, flatness, integrality and normality of the model at level $\Gamma_M(M,H)$, a smooth proper model at level $\Gamma_N(p,M,H)$, a curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field $\overline{F}_H$, the isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ with the geometric generic fibre, sections $\varepsilon^\infty$, the Atkin–Lehner isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.w$, the smooth locus, the special-fibre curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ with its two component maps $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,i$, $i \in \{0,1\}$, and the inclusion $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$); a level datum $\Lambda :$ `LevelData p M H hpM Pl`, consisting of $\sigma_A : \operatorname{Spec} \mathrm{Pl} \to$ `base p` with $\mathrm{barPt} \circ$-compatibility, a scheme $\Lambda.X$ with structure morphism $\Lambda.f$, a relative group law $\Lambda.L$, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$, $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$; and a Néron object $O :$ `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM Pl hPl Λ`, with scheme $O.G$, structure morphism $O.g$ over `base p`, commutative relative group law $O.L$, a bijection $O.\mathrm{pts} : J_H(M) \simeq$ `SchemeHomOver (genPt p) O.g` (where $J_H(M) =$ `JH M H` is $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $\overline{F}_H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) compatible with addition, Galois and the Hecke generators, the usual geometric properties of $O.g$, a finite set $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ of pairs of places of $\overline{F}_p :=$ `Fbar p M H hpM κ` $=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (ΓN p M H hpM)`, and the reduction bijection $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}$. Here `hrepΛ` asserts that the designation $(\Lambda.X, \Lambda.f)$ with the unit section of $\Lambda.L$ represents the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ functor, cut out by the fibrewise algebraic-equivalence-to-zero condition `algEquivZeroCut`, of the $\Gamma_N$-level model with rigidifying section $\varepsilon^\infty$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$. Finally, `O.finPts m` denotes the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by those $m$-torsion classes $x$ for which $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ satisfies the predicate `ExtendsToPlace Pl Λ.σA`.
--
--   Hypothesis groups. (i) Picard representability: `hD` asserts that $(O.G, O.g)$ with the unit section of $O.L$ represents the `algEquivZeroCut` subfunctor of the relative Picard functor of the $\Gamma_M$-level model over $R_p$ rigidified along $\varepsilon^\infty$; `hDQ` is the corresponding statement after base change to $\mathbb{Q}$, and `hsep` says that the base-changed curve is separated. (ii) Abel–Jacobi configuration: $\mathrm{ajQ}$ is a morphism of the $\mathbb{Q}$-curve into the base-changed designation over its structure morphism; `hajQε` says it carries the base-changed section $\varepsilon^\infty$ to the zero section; `hajQ` says that for every field $K$, every $t : \operatorname{Spec} K \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Q}$ and every $K$-point $x$ of the curve over $t$, the pullback along $x \cdot \mathrm{ajQ}$ of the Poincaré bundle of `hDQ` is isomorphic to the tensor product of the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ with the ideal module of the divisor of the point $t$ followed by the base-changed $\varepsilon^\infty$, i.e. $\mathrm{ajQ}$ is the Abel–Jacobi map $x \mapsto [(x) - (\varepsilon^\infty)]$; `hpoinc` identifies the Poincaré bundle of `hDQ` with the base change to $\mathbb{Q}$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hD` along the first projection of $O.g$. (iii) Comparison of generic fibres: $\mathrm{kQ}$ is a morphism from the fibre over `genPt p` to the fibre over $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Q}$ with `hkQ₁` and `hkQ₂` saying that it commutes with the first projection and induces $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Q}$ on the second; $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C \to O.G$ is required by `hajbar` to be $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by $\mathrm{kQ}$, $\mathrm{ajQ}$ and the first projection, and by `hajbar_over` to lie over `genPt p`; $\overline{\varepsilon}$ is a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$, with `hεbar` identifying it with the section $\varepsilon^\infty$ on the geometric generic fibre and `hεbar_aj` saying that $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ sends it to the origin of $O.L$. (iv) Compatibility of $O.\mathrm{pts}$ with the group law: `hpts_law` says $O.\mathrm{pts}(x+y)$ is the product of $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ and $O.\mathrm{pts}\,y$ for the relative group law attached to `hD` by `algEquivZeroGroupCut`. (v) Abel–Jacobi dictionary `hAJ`: for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ with $s$ satisfying the condition of `hεbar`, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ equal to $\mathrm{single}(\text{place of } x) - \mathrm{single}(\text{place of } s)$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$, with $(O.\mathrm{pts}\,[D_v])_1 = x \cdot \overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   (vi) The inertia-invariant ring: $R$ is a commutative ring which is a domain, Henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, an algebra over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with faithful scalar action, such that `hRA` places the image of $R$ inside $\mathrm{Pl}$, `hRdvr` makes $R$ a discrete valuation ring, `hRirr` makes $p$ irreducible in $R$, `hRfix` characterises the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Pl}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ as the automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $R$ pointwise, and `hRmax` says every element of $\mathrm{Pl}$ fixed by that inertia subgroup comes from $R$. (vii) The $p$-divisible group: $\mathcal{G} :$ [`PDivisibleGroup R p h`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199) (finite free cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebras $\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$ with surjective transitions, $\operatorname{rank} = p^{vh}$, kernels the $p^v$-torsion ideals), together with an additive map $\Delta$ from $\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{Points}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $J_H(M)$ which is injective (`hΔinj`), whose image at level $v$ is exactly `O.finPts (p ^ v)` (`hΔlev`), which is Galois-equivariant for automorphisms $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $R$-algebra automorphisms $\tau'$ agreeing with them (`hΔgal`), and which intertwines, for every set $S$ and every Hecke generator $g$ of [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13), a transition-compatible family of coalgebra endomorphisms $\varphi_v$ of the levels with the operator `genOpH M H S g` on $J_H(M)$ (`hΔhecke`). (viii) Atkin–Lehner: $w_{\mathrm{gen}}$ is a semilinear automorphism of $\overline{F}_H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a pair of ring automorphisms compatible with the structure map), and `hwgen` says that if a point $y'$ composed with $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, the first projection and $\mathfrak{X}.w$ agrees with $y$ composed with $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first projection, then the place of $y'$ is $w_{\mathrm{gen}}$ applied to the place of $y$; $\overline{W}$ is an additive endomorphism of $J_H(M)$ with $\overline{W}x = w_{\mathrm{gen}} \cdot x$ (`hWbar`). (ix) The structure map at $\mathrm{Pl}$: $\rho : R_p \to \mathrm{Pl}$ with `hρ` saying that $\rho$ followed by the inclusion is the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and `hσA : Λ.σA = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ρ)`.
--
--   (x) The two-point reduction dictionary `hsp` (hypotheses summarised here): for each $i \in \{0,1\}$, given two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y_1, y_2$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$, lifts $u_1, u_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathrm{Pl}$ of these points whose images lie in the smooth locus, reductions $u_{\kappa,1}, u_{\kappa,2}$ to the fibre over $\kappa$ compatible with the $u_j$ and sections of the fibre, closed points $P_1, P_2$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ lying on the $i$-th component above the reductions, a degree-zero divisor $D_v = \mathrm{single}(\text{place of } y_1) - \mathrm{single}(\text{place of } y_2)$, and an admissible gluing datum $x$ (a pair of degree-zero divisors of $\overline{F}_p$ over $\kappa$ together with a function on $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ with values in $\mathrm{Additive}\,\kappa^\times$, the divisors vanishing at the respective places of each pair) whose first component is $\mathrm{single}(\text{place of } P_1) - \mathrm{single}(\text{place of } P_2)$ if $i = 0$ and $0$ otherwise, whose second component is that difference if $i = 1$ and $0$ otherwise, and whose third component is $0$: then there is a section $s$ of $O.g$ over $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ with $(O.\mathrm{pts}\,[D_v])_1 = \mathrm{barPt}\,\mathrm{Pl} \cdot s$ and $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ of the restriction of $s$ along $\mathrm{resPt}\,\mathrm{Pl}$ equal to the class of $x$ in `GluedPic0 κ (Fbar …) O.ssFinset`.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $x$ in the $p$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \overline{F}_H)$ whose underlying class lies in `O.finPts p`, for every degree-zero divisor $D$ of $\overline{F}_H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $f \in \overline{F}_H$ and every Laurent series $y$ over $\mathrm{Pl}$ such that $[D] = x$, $f \neq 0$, $p \cdot (w_{\mathrm{gen}} \cdot D)(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ for every place $v$ of $\overline{F}_H$ (so that $\operatorname{div} f = p\,(w_{\mathrm{gen}} D)$), the Laurent series of $f$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$ under $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is non-zero, and for every $g \in \overline{F}_p$ whose Laurent series is that reduction and with $p \mid \operatorname{ord}_v(g)$ at every place $v$ of $\overline{F}_p$ over $\kappa$: there exist $k \in \mathbb{N}$, a function $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,k \to \mathrm{Fin}\,2$, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y(i)$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$, lifts $u(i)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{ofHom}\,\rho)$ of the $\Gamma_M$-level model, morphisms $u_\kappa(i)$ from $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ to the fibre of the model along the residue map composed with $\rho$, closed points $P(i)$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$, integers $n(i)$, a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ of $\overline{F}_H$, an admissible gluing datum $x_g$ for $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$, and a degree-zero divisor $E$ of $\overline{F}_p$ over $\kappa$, such that:
--
--   1. for every $i$, $\mathrm{barPt}\,\mathrm{Pl}$ followed by $u(i)$ equals $y(i)$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first projection (each $u(i)$ lifts $y(i)$);
--
--   2. for every $i$, the image of $u(i)$ on points is contained in $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$;
--
--   3. for every $i$, $u_\kappa(i)$ followed by the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map followed by $u(i)$;
--
--   4. for every $i$, $u_\kappa(i)$ followed by the second projection is the identity;
--
--   5. for every $i$, the closed point $P(i)$ is carried by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ followed by the component map $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}(c(i))$ to the image of the closed point of $\kappa$ under $u_\kappa(i)$;
--
--   6. $\sum_{c(i) = 0} n(i) = 0$;
--
--   7. $\sum_{c(i) = 1} n(i) = 0$;
--
--   8. $D_v = \sum_i n(i)\,\mathrm{single}(\text{place of } y(i))$, the places taken under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$;
--
--   9. the first component of $x_g$ is $\sum_{c(i)=0} n(i)\,\mathrm{single}(\text{place of } P(i))$;
--
--   10. the second component of $x_g$ is $\sum_{c(i)=1} n(i)\,\mathrm{single}(\text{place of } P(i))$;
--
--   11. the third component of $x_g$ is $0$;
--
--   12. $[D_v] = \overline{W}x$ in $J_H(M)$;
--
--   13. $[E]$ equals the first coordinate of `GluedPic0.toPic0Pair O.ssFinset` applied to the class of $x_g$;
--
--   14. $p \cdot E(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(g)$ for every place $v$ of $\overline{F}_p$ over $\kappa$.
--
--   This is the construction, at a place above $p$ on the Deligne–Rapoport type model of $X_H(M)$ with $p \parallel M$, of a configured divisor representing the Atkin–Lehner translate of a $p$-torsion class in the finite part: the representing divisor is supported on points reducing into the smooth locus, its support is split according to the two components of the special fibre with each partial degree zero, and the resulting gluing datum has $\Sigma^\infty$-component equal to $\tfrac1p \operatorname{div}(g)$ for the reduced root $g$. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_section_toPic0Pair_eq_mk_of_mem_finPts_of_forall_dvd_ord_tauFree`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_section_toPic0Pair_eq_mk_of_mem_finPts_of_forall_dvd_ord_tauFree), where it is combined with the reduction dictionary for configured sums to compute the $\Sigma^\infty$-coordinate of the reduction of the class.
